From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:09:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: decide when an idle external DCP may
 power down

A T8132 external display coprocessor (dcpext) keeps its CPU running
and its firmware DART and dispext CPU, frontend and system domains
powered as long as the machine is up, also with nothing attached:
its only power-down runs for a sleep that powers the SoC down.

Nothing needs it then. A display only appears through the AP: the
HDMI port's hot-plug GPIO or a Type-C route, and each of them asks
the firmware to connect first. Add the pure decision for powering an
idle dcpext down, for the KUnit suite:
- never with the knob at 0, without the board's power-down or on a
  failed session; nothing to do once it is down;
- not yet while its session or DPTX service is starting, the HDMI
  output is starting, a Type-C reconnect is queued, teardown calls
  are unanswered, a call or swap is in flight, or the system is
  sleeping: look again after the delay;
- not while anything is attached (a DPTX port connected, a Type-C
  route, HDMI hot-plug high, a sink reported, the display or its
  DART on): the event that removes it looks again;
- else power it down.
The delay knob is kept within 1 s to 10 min; 0 turns it off.

New KUnit suite apple-dcp-m4-ext-idle (6 cases).

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/Makefile               |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-ext-idle-test.c | 161 +++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-ext-idle.h      | 134 +++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 296 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-ext-idle-test.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-ext-idle.h

